# Files kept OUT of the public mirror.
#
# `git archive HEAD` honours `export-ignore`, and the public mirror is
# built by `npx tsx scripts/public-export.ts`, which archives HEAD — so
# anything marked here is in the private repo and not in the published
# tree.
#
# Why these four: they are the machinery for publishing this repo FROM a
# private upstream, which is meaningless to anyone who clones the public
# mirror — there is no private tree on the other side to de-identify.
#
# And they are the one place that necessarily CONTAINS the identifiers
# they ban: the maintainer's username and company email domain are
# written out as match rules. Shipping those in one file lets anyone
# reconstruct the work address that the GitHub-noreply commit identity
# exists to keep off the public record. A de-identification guard that
# publishes the identifiers is worse than no guard, so it stays private
# and runs here, where the tree it protects actually is.
#
# Do not restate those rules in a comment anywhere that ships. The first
# version of THIS comment quoted them verbatim, and the guard did not
# catch it: a regex source escapes the identifier (a word-boundary
# marker before it, a backslash inside the domain), which is exactly
# what the guard's own word-boundary and literal-dot matching then fail
# to see. Describe them; never spell them.
scripts/_public-release.ts        export-ignore
scripts/_public-release.test.ts   export-ignore
scripts/public-export.ts          export-ignore
scripts/public-export.test.ts     export-ignore
